  "goodToKnow": "Der Schnabel is a beak or bill. Colloquially, it's the mouth: Halt den Schnabel! (shut up!). Reden, wie einem der Schnabel gewachsen ist means to speak plainly, as one naturally talks; Martin Luther said translators should listen to how ordinary people speak, dem Volk aufs Maul schauen. Das Schnabeltier is a platypus (beak animal). Plural: die Schnäbel."
